    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0225" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/6–645</note>
                <head>No. 52 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        Marshal Stalin to Prime
                        Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation?]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">personal</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-05">June 5, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arising from your message<anchor n="2" xml:id="d52-f2"/> on the desirability of
                    transferring meeting of the Three to an earlier date than July 15th, I should
                    like to say once again that the date of July 15th was proposed by President
                        Truman; and I expressed agreement
                    with that date. Inasmuch as correspondence is taking place between you and
                    President Truman on this subject at the
                    moment, I shall refrain from making any new proposals about the date of our
                    meeting.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
